            // Experience
            section#experience.resume-section
               .resume-section-content
                    h2.mb-5 Experience

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Senior Member of Technical Staff (Project Lead)
                            .subheading.mb-3 Oracle Cloud Infrastructure, Seattle &mdash; Repair Management / Object Storage
                            ul
                                li Led a customer-facing link repair initiative, defining process flows and aligning engineering, operations, and support teams on resolution strategy.
                            p.font-italic.mb-2 Senior Member of Technical Staff &ndash; Software Developer, Object Storage Metadata Service
                            ul
                                li Designed a rebalancing and resharding solution based on customer load to dynamically balance buckets and objects across shards.
                                li Delivered critical customer features including Archive Tier Sunset and Embargo for all customer APIs, and improved list API latency by implementing an automated index-rebuild.
                                li Spearheaded the strategic sunset of the OCI Archive Tier, orchestrating the migration of all legacy resources to Standard and Infrequent Access tiers, simplifying storage tiering, improving metering, and reducing long-term operational complexity.
                                li Improved developer productivity by leading a repo split and JDK 17 upgrade for the object storage monolithic codebase.
                                li Led a team of 5 engineers across the US and IDC, orchestrating the decoupling of monolithic repositories and services and directing the deployment of critical metadata infrastructure; spearheaded a high-priority task force to drive the enterprise-wide migration from Java 8 to Java 17, ensuring security compliance and performance optimization.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary February 2021 - Present

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Software Developer Intern
                            .subheading.mb-3 Amazon Web Services, Seattle &mdash; AWS EC2 Security
                            ul
                                li Designed an end-to-end architecture to enhance customer security by removing outdated data stored in S3 buckets.
                                li Provided an API and CLI option for clients to set the number of days they want data to be stored.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary June 2020 - August 2020

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Technical Analyst
                            .subheading.mb-3 Goldman Sachs, Bengaluru &mdash; Document Lake, Pricing Technology
                            p Document Lake is a centralized internal platform for storing documents in Elastic Cloud Storage (ECS), providing search and OCR capabilities.
                            ul
                                li Conceived and implemented the plan to migrate an older system to Document Lake; the migrated system processes up to 10 million files and 1TB of data per day, improving throughput by over 80% versus the older system.
                                li Brainstormed and devised a scalable multithreaded solution using Kafka to migrate files to the cloud using Amazon S3.
                                li Improvised the migration plan by introducing MongoDB as a staging table to store Kafka offsets and added the ability to replay retained messages from a topic, exposed as a secure REST endpoint via SwaggerUI.
                                li Developed a Proof of Concept comparing Elasticsearch query retrieval time and complex query support against ECS's built-in bucket search; designed data models, RESTful microservices and configured Elasticsearch clusters.
                                li Onboarded feeds to EMS (Enterprise Messaging System) Queues, Streams and hybrid pipeline/stream systems that transport vendor data to the primary database.
                                li Designed Prime View, a UI for operations to view and perform real-time updates to trading data.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary June 2017 - April 2019

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between.mb-5
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Summer Intern
                            .subheading.mb-3 Goldman Sachs, Bengaluru &mdash; DataFactory
                            ul
                                li Developed the Tasks UI in AngularJS2 to gather input from Operations, replacing the previous email-based process.
                                li Streamlined the process by generating tasks at runtime and delegating them to maintain a timely response.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary May 2016 - June 2016

                    .d-flex.flex-column.flex-md-row.justify-content-between
                        .flex-grow-1
                            h3.mb-0 Software Developer Intern / Algorithmic Problem Setter
                            .subheading.mb-3 GeeksforGeeks, Noida
                            ul
                                li Added new features to practice.geeksforgeeks.org and created new algorithmic problems for their contests.
                                li Taught algorithms and data structures in offline Geeks classes and managed their live online courses, which had over 3500+ students.
                        .flex-shrink-0
                            span.text-primary Dec 2015 - Jan 2015, Apr 2019 - Jul 2019

